:: StoryJavaScript [script]
window.Engine = SugarCube.Engine;

$(document).on(':passageprocess', function () {
  // Clean up any running timers when navigating to a new passage
  if (window.typewriterInterval) {
    clearInterval(window.typewriterInterval);
    window.typewriterInterval = null;
  }
  if (window.hallucinationTimer) {
    clearInterval(window.hallucinationTimer);
    window.hallucinationTimer = null;
  }
});

window.revealGrade = function () {
  var container = document.getElementById("grade-reveal");
  if (container) {
    container.innerHTML = `
      <div class="end-card end-bad">
        <h3 style="color: #ff5555; margin-top: 0;">BAD ENDING: Cognitive Atrophy</h3>
        <p style="color: #ddd; font-size: 1.1em;">You score a 12% on the final exam. Because you outsourced your thinking to a machine for months, you failed to learn the skills you came to school for. The real world doesn't always let you bring a chatbot to the test.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <button onclick="SugarCube.Engine.restart()" class="btn btn-neutral">Restart Story</button>
      </div>
    `;
  }
};

:: Start
<div class="container">
  <h1>The AI Dilemma</h1>

  <div id="typewriter" style="min-height: 120px; color: #00ff00; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 1.1em; background: #050505; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 25px; box-shadow: inset 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.8); white-space: pre-wrap;"></div>

  <<script>>
    $(document).one(':passagedisplay', function () {
      var text = "TIME: 11:42 PM.\nDEADLINE: 8:00 AM.\nSTATUS: 0 words written.\n\nYour final History essay on Cold War Geopolitics is completely blank.";
      var i = 0;
      var tw = document.getElementById("typewriter");
      if (!tw) return;
      
      if (window.typewriterInterval) {
        clearInterval(window.typewriterInterval);
      }
      
      window.typewriterInterval = setInterval(function () {
        if (i < text.length) {
          tw.innerHTML += text.charAt(i) === '\n' ? '<br>' : text.charAt(i);
          i++;
        } else {
          clearInterval(window.typewriterInterval);
          window.typewriterInterval = null;
        }
      }, 30);
    });
  <</script>>

  <p>
    The quiet hum of your laptop's cooling fan is the only sound in the suffocating stillness of your dorm room. Outside, a gentle rain taps against the glass, reflecting the cold amber glow of the campus streetlights. But inside, your focus is locked onto a glowing white screen. The cursor blinks with mocking regularity on the blank Google Doc. You haven't opened the history textbook all semester, and the syllabus's stern warnings from Professor Vance echo in your mind: no late submissions, no excuses, and a zero on this paper means failing the entire course.
  </p>
  <p>
    Just a click away, in another browser tab, is "Apex-AI"—a sleek, advanced artificial intelligence assistant. Its interface is minimalist, welcoming, and unbelievably fast. It stands ready, a silent digital ghost, offering to vaporize your panic with a flawless, instantaneous 1,500-word analysis of Truman's containment strategy. The temptation is a heavy, physical ache in your chest. You can hear your own rapid heartbeat. 
  </p>
  <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #a5b4fc;">
    The clock is ticking, and the night is young but dwindling. How will you navigate this academic crucible?
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 25px;">
    <a data-passage="The Hard Way" class="btn btn-neutral">Brew coffee and write it yourself (The Hard Way)</a>
    <a data-passage="The Tutor Way" class="btn btn-purple">Ask the AI to explain the concepts so you can write it (The Middle Path)</a>
    <a data-passage="The Easy Way" class="btn btn-danger">Paste the prompt into the AI and copy the result (The Easy Way)</a>
    <a data-passage="Request Extension" class="btn">Email Professor Vance at 12:00 AM (Request Extension)</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Request Extension
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Last-Minute Request</h2>
  <p>
    Your fingers hover uncertainly over the keys as you open your university email client. The blue light casts long shadows across your desk. You begin to compose a message to Professor Vance, trying to walk an impossibly thin tightrope: you need to sound deeply apologetic, genuinely overwhelmed by "unforeseen personal emergencies," yet completely professional and respectful. You revise the subject line three times before settling on *HECO 302: Urgent Inquiry Regarding Essay Submission*.
  </p>
  <p>
    "Dear Professor Vance," you write, your heart hammering against your ribs, "I am writing to humbly request a brief 24-hour extension on our final essay..." You hit 'Send' at exactly 12:05 AM. The email vanishes into the digital ether. You know that Professor Vance—an academic traditionalist who grades with a fountain pen and wakes up at dawn—is almost certainly fast asleep. There is no automated confirmation, no guaranteed safety net. Only the silent wait.
  </p>
  <p>
    The clock now reads 12:06 AM. The heavy silence of your room rushes back to fill the void. What is your plan while you wait for a reply that might never come, or might be a crushing rejection?
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="The Hard Way" class="btn btn-neutral">Don't risk it. Start writing it yourself immediately (The Hard Way).</a>
    <a data-passage="The Tutor Way" class="btn btn-purple">Use the AI tutor to draft an outline just in case (The Middle Path).</a>
    <a data-passage="Oversleep Risk" class="btn btn-danger">Go to sleep and hope he is merciful in the morning.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Oversleep Risk
<div class="container">
  <h2>A Cold Awakening</h2>
  <p>
    Deciding to trust in human mercy, you close your laptop, kick off your shoes, and collapse onto your bed. But sleep is not a sanctuary. You toss and turn, trapped in a feverish, fitful cycle of nightmares where giant red letters drift across endless blank pages, and Professor Vance's stern voice echoes from the shadows of a towering lecture hall.
  </p>
  <p>
    You wake up with a violent jolt, your chest gasping for air. The room is flooded with bright, unforgiving morning sunlight. You grab your phone. The screen illuminates: <strong>7:30 AM!</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Panic, cold and sharp, paralyzes you. You have exactly thirty minutes. With trembling, sweaty hands, you refresh your student inbox. A new email from Professor Vance, sent at 7:10 AM, glares back at you:
  </p>
  <div class="ai-text" style="border-left-color: #888; color: #ddd; font-family: sans-serif;">
    "Dear Student,<br><br>
    As clearly outlined in the syllabus, extensions are only granted for documented medical emergencies or when requested at least 24 hours in advance. To maintain fairness for your peers, the submission portal closes at 8:00 AM sharp, and late work cannot be accepted under any circumstances.<br><br>
    Best,<br>
    Prof. Vance"
  </div>
  <p>
    The words swim before your eyes. Thirty minutes. Zero words written. The portal is a ticking time bomb. The abyss of an automatic course failure is staring right at you.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="The Easy Way" class="btn btn-danger">Panic-paste the prompt into the AI and submit the raw result.</a>
    <a data-passage="Honest Failure" class="btn btn-neutral">Submit a blank document and accept the zero.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: The Hard Way
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Long Night</h2>
  <p>
    With a sudden surge of resolve, you close the tempting Apex-AI browser tab. The screen blinks, and the digital phantom is gone. It's just you, the intimidatingly thick textbook *A Bipolar Century*, and the soft, steady hum of the coffee maker heating up in the corner. You pour a steaming mug of black coffee, the dark, bitter aroma filling the air and clearing the initial fog from your brain.
  </p>
  <p>
    You open the massive textbook. The pages are crisp and heavy. You realize that to write 1,500 words before the sun rises, you cannot afford to wander aimlessly through fifty years of history. You must be precise. You need a razor-sharp, compelling thesis that will guide your research and keep you focused through the exhausting hours ahead.
  </p>
  <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #a5b4fc;">
    Which core geopolitical event of the Cold War will you build your entire paper around?
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Hard Way Topic" class="btn" style="border-color: #81c784; color: #81c784;">Focus on European Containment (The Berlin Airlift, 1948)</a>
    <a data-passage="Hard Way Topic" class="btn" style="border-color: #a64dff; color: #a64dff;">Focus on Brinkmanship & Proxy Conflicts (The Cuban Missile Crisis, 1962)</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Hard Way Topic
<div class="container">
  <h2>The 3:00 AM Fatigue</h2>
  <p>
    You choose your focal point, plant your thesis firmly at the end of the introductory paragraph, and begin to write. The clock on your wall crawls forward with agonizing deliberation. The click-clack of your keys feels incredibly loud in the sleeping dorm.
  </p>
  <p>
    By the time the clock strikes 3:00 AM, the silence of the night is absolute, broken only by the rhythmic, mocking tick of the wall clock. You look at your word counter: 700 words. You're not even halfway there. Your eyelids feel like lead weights, your shoulders are knotted with tension, and the sentences you are writing are beginning to read like incoherent, repetitive mud.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your brain is screaming for rest, and in the dark corner of your mind, the whispering temptation of the AI tool returns. You could open it, paste your draft, and let it finish the rest in five seconds.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Fatigue Push" class="btn">Chug an energy drink and push through the fatigue.</a>
    <a data-passage="Power Nap" class="btn btn-neutral">Set an alarm for a 30-minute power nap.</a>
    <a data-passage="The Easy Way" class="btn btn-danger">Give up and open the AI tab to finish it.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Fatigue Push
<div class="container">
  <h2>Caffeine-Fueled Frenzy</h2>
  <p>
    You stand up, stretch your aching limbs, and walk to the mini-fridge. You pull out a highly concentrated, neon-colored energy drink from the back shelf and crack it open. The sharp, artificial citrus scent hits you instantly. You gulp it down, the ice-cold, sugary carbonation shocking your throat and making your eyes water.
  </p>
  <p>
    Within fifteen minutes, the chemical cocktail surges into your bloodstream. Your heart begins to strike a rapid, frantic rhythm against your ribs. Your pupils dilate, and a sudden, jittery heat washes over your body. You sit back down, and your fingers begin to fly across the keyboard like possessed spiders.
  </p>
  <p>
    You weave a chaotic, intense, but incredibly detailed analysis. You pull together primary quotes from the textbook, breaking down Truman's rhetoric and Soviet counter-moves. The vocabulary is raw and the structure is slightly unpolished, but it is real, genuine history. At exactly 7:45 AM, the word counter clicks past 1,500. Your hands are shaking, your eyes are bloodshot, and you feel like a hollowed-out ghost—but the work is completely, undeniably yours.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Caffeine Essay Submission" class="btn btn-success">Submit the caffeine-fueled paper.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Caffeine Essay Submission
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Verdict</h2>
  <p>
    You upload the document to the university portal at 7:52 AM, watching the progress bar crawl to 100% with your breath held. The green checkmark appears: *Submission Successful*. You close your laptop, fall face-first onto your unmade bed, and sink into a heavy, dreamless blackout sleep that lasts until the late afternoon.
  </p>
  <p>
    A week later, the notification pings on your phone. You log in to view your grade, your throat tightening with anxiety. You see it: <strong style="color: #81c784;">B- (81%)</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You scroll down to read the feedback. Professor Vance has left a handwritten digital note in bright red:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #aaa; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding: 15px; border-left: 3px solid #81c784; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.6;">
    "A highly energetic and incredibly detailed paper. It suffers from some organizational chaos and structural wandering in the second half—likely the result of a late-night push—but your core analysis of Cold War power dynamics is remarkably sharp and authentic. Genuine, commendable effort."
  </p>
  <p>
    A wave of pure, sweet relief washes over you. You survived. More importantly, the grueling struggle forced you to actually engage with the history, mapping the arguments deep into your own mind.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Final Exam Prepared" class="btn">Fast forward to the Final Exam...</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Power Nap
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Sleep Trap</h2>
  <p>
    You convince yourself that a brief rest is the only way to save your failing cognitive faculties. "Just thirty minutes," you mutter, setting a loud, repeating alarm on your phone and placing it right next to your pillow. You rest your heavy head on the cool, hard wooden surface of your desk, intending to close your eyes for just a moment of peace.
  </p>
  <p>
    The darkness is immediate and absolute. You fall into a deep, heavy slumber, completely divorced from reality.
  </p>
  <p>
    ...
  </p>
  <p>
    You wake up with a sudden, panicked gasp. The room is no longer dark; it is fully illuminated by the harsh, golden rays of the morning sun. Birds are chirping cheerfully outside. Your heart drops into your stomach as you grab your phone. The screen blinks: <strong>7:15 AM!</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    The alarm had gone off, but in your state of total physical exhaustion, your hand must have automatically swiped it off without your conscious mind ever registering it. The submission portal locks forever in exactly 45 minutes, and your essay stands half-finished at a miserable 700 words.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Late Scramble" class="btn btn-neutral">Scramble to write whatever you can in 45 minutes and submit it late.</a>
    <a data-passage="The Easy Way" class="btn btn-danger">Panic and use the AI to write the whole thing in 15 minutes.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: Late Scramble
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Mad Dash</h2>
  <p>
    You reject the temptation to cheat. You open the half-finished document, put your fingers on the keyboard, and begin to type like an absolute maniac. There is no time to double-check dates, consult the index, or craft elegant transitions. You rely entirely on your raw memory of the lectures, typing out whatever you can recall about the Iron Curtain, containment, and Berlin.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your fingers blur across the keyboard. You manage to drag the word count up to 1,000 words. At exactly 8:15 AM—fifteen minutes after the official deadline—your trembling finger clicks the submit button. The system logs it with a bright red warning: *LATE SUBMISSION*.
  </p>
  <p>
    A week later, you receive your graded paper. You got a <strong style="color: #ffaa00;">C- (70%)</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Professor Vance leaves a comment at the bottom:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #aaa; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding: 15px; border-left: 3px solid #ffaa00; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.6;">
    "The content you managed to produce shows a very solid, commendable grasp of the foundational geopolitical tensions. However, it is far too brief and lacks necessary scholarly depth. Combined with a mandatory 15% late penalty for missing the 8:00 AM deadline, this is the best I can award. I appreciate that you did the work yourself."
  </p>
  <p>
    It is a painful blow to your GPA, but as you stare at the C-, you feel a quiet, stubborn pride. You didn't take the cowards' way out.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Final Exam Prepared" class="btn">Fast forward to the Final Exam...</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: The Tutor Way
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Interactive Tutor</h2>
  <p>
    You decide to use the power of Apex-AI, but you make a conscious pact with yourself: you will not let the machine write for you. You will use it to learn. You open the chat tab and type a carefully structured prompt:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); padding: 12px; border-left: 3px solid #a64dff; border-radius: 4px;">
    "Act as an expert history tutor. Explain the geopolitical impacts of the early Cold War like I'm a beginner, and provide a comprehensive 5-point conceptual outline for a 1,500-word academic essay on containment."
  </p>
  <p>
    The AI responds almost instantly, its cursor generating text with lightning speed:
  </p>
  <div class="ai-text">
    AI: "I would be delighted to help you master this material! Think of the early Cold War not as a random series of events, but as a high-stakes global chess match between two grandmasters with entirely incompatible worldviews—the United States and the Soviet Union. Because direct confrontation meant nuclear annihilation, they fought along the margins. Here is a conceptual outline designed to structure a compelling, high-scoring essay:<br><br>
    <strong>1. Introduction & The Grand Strategy:</strong> Defining Bipolarity and the Containment doctrine.<br>
    <strong>2. The Divided Continent:</strong> The physical and ideological reality of Churchill's 'Iron Curtain'.<br>
    <strong>3. The Economic Shield:</strong> The Truman Doctrine and the Marshall Plan as economic containment.<br>
    <strong>4. Proxy Battlegrounds:</strong> How local conflicts (like the Berlin Blockade) represented global tensions.<br>
    <strong>5. The Legacy:</strong> How early containment institutionalized a bipolar global order."
  </div>
  <p>
    The outline is incredibly clear and logical. But before it stops, the AI adds a final paragraph:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #a5b4fc; font-weight: 600;">
    "Before we draft our thesis, let's test your understanding of the core dynamics. In 1948, what was the primary geopolitical reason the Soviet Union blocked all land access to West Berlin?"
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="TutorQuizCurrency" class="btn btn-neutral">"To stop the US from introducing currency reforms and economically consolidating West Germany."</a>
    <a data-passage="TutorQuizClash" class="btn btn-neutral">"To provoke a direct military confrontation and start World War III."</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: TutorQuizCurrency
<div class="container">
  <h2>Academic Praise</h2>
  <div class="ai-text">
    AI: "Brilliant! That is absolutely correct. It was a calculated economic and political blockade designed to protest the unilateral introduction of the Deutsche Mark and the consolidation of the Western zones. Stalin wanted to force the West's hand economically, not invite a direct military World War III. This level of historical nuance is exactly what separates a generic essay from an outstanding, A-grade paper! Let's build a sophisticated thesis based on this insight..."
  </div>
  <p>
    Reading the AI's enthusiastic response ignites a sudden spark of academic confidence in your chest. The historical concepts aren't just dry names and dates anymore—they are active, fascinating pieces of a global puzzle. You feel fully locked into the zone, ready to tackle the writing.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
