:: Tutor Nuance
<div class="container">
  <h2>Nuance and Understanding</h2>
  <p>
    Sensing an opportunity to elevate your paper even further, you type another question:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); padding: 12px; border-left: 3px solid #a64dff; border-radius: 4px;">
    "How exactly did the economic aid of the Marshall Plan integrate with the political strategy of containment? Were they separate policies or part of the same grand strategy?"
  </p>
  <div class="ai-text">
    AI: "Excellent question! They were actually two sides of the very same coin. Containment (as codified by the Truman Doctrine) was the political and military promise to halt Soviet expansion wherever it occurred. The Marshall Plan was the massive economic engine that made that promise viable. By pumping billions of dollars to rebuild the shattered infrastructures of Western Europe, the United States ensured these nations remained economically stable and prosperous—thus making them completely immune to the hunger, despair, and political chaos that typically fuel domestic communist revolutions."
  </div>
  <p>
    This brilliant distinction is the final piece of the puzzle. You close the chat tab, open your processor, and spend the next four hours typing furiously. But you aren't copy-pasting. You are writing in your own voice, utilizing concepts that you now genuinely, deeply understand.
  </p>
  <p>
    You submit a beautifully crafted, highly sophisticated 1,500-word paper at exactly 4:30 AM, hours before the deadline.
  </p>
  <p>
    A week later, you receive your graded paper: an <strong style="color: #81c784;">A (95%)</strong>. Professor Vance leaves a glowing, rare comment at the bottom:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #aaa; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding: 15px; border-left: 3px solid #81c784; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.6;">
    "An absolutely outstanding essay. Your analysis of the precise synergy between the military containment of the Truman Doctrine and the economic machinery of the Marshall Plan is graduate-level work. Exceptionally well-researched and beautifully written. Brilliant."
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
