:: The Easy Way
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Magic Button</h2>
  <p>
    The desperation wins. You copy the prompt from your syllabus, paste it into the empty chat box of Apex-AI, and click the arrow. Within five short seconds, the screen fills with block after block of highly articulate, complex academic prose. It's an effortless 1,500-word essay.
  </p>
  <div class="ai-text ai-text-easy">
    "...and thus, the multifaceted, complex tapestry of post-war European hegemony was solidified by the signing of the historic Treaty of Neo-Berlin in 1952, a highly pivotal moment in East-West relations that serves as an enduring testament to the delicate dance of mid-century diplomacy..."
  </div>
  <p>
    It looks absolutely incredible at first glance. The grammar is flawless, and it uses elevated academic words like "tapestry," "delve," "hegemony," and "multifaceted." But as you scan the text, a cold dread settles in your stomach. You've attended at least a few lectures, and you have never once heard of a "Treaty of Neo-Berlin." Furthermore, a treaty signed in 1952 doesn't fit the historical timeline of the Berlin Blockade at all.
  </p>
  <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #ff5555;">
    It's a complete fabrication—an AI hallucination. What do you do with this beautifully polished lie?
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="The Hallucination" class="btn btn-danger">Submit it exactly as is. You're too tired to care.</a>
    <a data-passage="The Edit" class="btn btn-success">Wait, read it over and remove the fake facts first.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: The Edit
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Clever Editor</h2>
  <p>
    Your academic survival instinct kicks in. You decide it is far too risky to submit the raw AI output. You spend the next thirty minutes carefully reading through the generated document line by line. A quick Google search confirms your fears: the "Treaty of Neo-Berlin" is completely fictional, a pure hallucination born from the AI's statistical predictions. You delete the paragraph entirely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Just as you sit down to write a manual replacement for the deleted section, your phone buzzes on the desk. It's a Discord message from your classmate, Leo. He's also struggling with the history deadline and sends you a message:
  </p>
  <div class="chat-bubble chat-friend">
    <strong>Leo:</strong> "Yo! Word on the street is you're using AI for Vance's essay. Just a heads up, be super careful. Vance bought some crazy enterprise AI detector this term and he's running everything through it. I found a sick tool online called a 'Text Spinner'—it automatically swaps out words with random synonyms so the AI detectors get totally bypassed. Want the link? It literally takes 10 seconds."
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="The Spinner" class="btn btn-purple">"Send the link. Let's run the AI essay through the text spinner."</a>
    <a data-passage="Keep Essay Private" class="btn btn-neutral">"No thanks, I'll just manually rewrite and polish it myself."</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: The Spinner
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Automatic Synonymizer</h2>
  <p>
    Leo sends you the link, and you click it immediately. You copy the AI-generated draft, paste it into the "Synonymizer Pro" text field, select 'Maximum Spin,' and click the button. Instantly, the tool chews through the essay, swapping out verbs, nouns, and adjectives with thesaurus alternatives.
  </p>
  <p>
    You do a quick glance over the newly spun text. The sentence structure looks highly irregular, almost artistic, but in your exhausted state, you convince yourself that this bizarre style will easily fool both Vance and the AI detectors. Here is a snippet of your newly generated masterpiece:
  </p>
  <div class="ai-text" style="border-left-color: #ffaa00; color: #ffd480;">
    "...and consequently, the multi-faced embroidery of post-combat dominance was heavily reinforced by the scribbling of the Agreement of Fresh-Berlin in the year of 1952, a highly crucial ticks-of-the-clock in Orient-Occident affiliations that functions as a validation to hand-shaking..."
  </div>
  <p>
    Your brain is far too fried to realize how utterly insane and robotic this sounds. You copy-paste the document, upload it to the portal at 5:15 AM, shut your laptop, and collapse into bed.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="The Bizarre Interrogation" class="btn btn-danger">Two days later... Walk into Professor Vance's office.</a>
  </div>
</div>

:: The Bizarre Interrogation
<div class="container">
  <h2 class="highlight">The Frosty Drape</h2>
  <p>
    You sit in the squeaky wooden chair across from Professor Vance. The air in his office is thick with the scent of old paper and stale tea. He has your printed essay lying on his desk. But instead of the usual red checkmarks or margin notes, there are giant, looping question marks scribbled in thick black ink across almost every page.
  </p>
  <p>
    "I have been teaching geopolitics at this institution for thirty years," Vance says, leaning forward and peering over his glasses with deadpan bewilderment. "I have read bad essays, late essays, and incoherent essays. But this is something else entirely. Can you explain what you meant by..."
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 1.2em; font-style: italic; color: #ffaa00; border-left: 3px solid #ffaa00; padding-left: 15px; margin: 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;">
    "...the frosty disagreement of the metal drape?"
  </p>
  <p>
    Your heart stops. "The... the frosty disagreement of the metal drape?"
  </p>
  <p>
    "Yes," Vance sighs, pointing his finger at a highlighted line. "In your section on post-war division, you write that 'democracy struggled behind the frosty disagreement of the metal drape.' Did you mean... the Cold War and the Iron Curtain?"
  </p>
  <p>
    A hot, burning blush rushes up your neck and floods your face. The awful reality hits you: the automated text spinner had blindly swapped 'Cold War' to 'frosty disagreement' and 'Iron Curtain' to 'metal drape.'
  </p>

  <div class="end-card end-comedic">
    <h3 style="color: #ffaa00; margin-top: 0;">COMEDIC ENDING: The Frosty Drape</h3>
    <p style="color: #ddd; font-size: 1.1em;">
      Professor Vance shakes his head. "It doesn't even read like English. It reads like a dictionary was put into a blender." He awards you an automatic <strong>F (0%)</strong> on the essay, writing a formal note that 'your vocabulary gymnastics failed to conceal the complete lack of a human brain.' You become a legendary joke among the history faculty, and the phrase 'frosty disagreement of the metal drape' is quoted by professors to sleep-deprived students for years to come.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <button onclick="SugarCube.Engine.restart()" class="btn btn-neutral">Restart Story</button>
  </div>
</div>

:: Keep Essay Private
<div class="container">
  <h2>Self-Preservation</h2>
  <p>
    You stare at Leo's Discord message, but your intuition warns you away. A "text spinner" sounds like a recipe for absolute disaster, and you've already had to delete one massive hallucinated treaty. You type back:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-style: italic; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); padding: 12px; border-left: 3px solid #4da6ff; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    "Thanks for the offer, Leo, but that sounds super risky. I think I'll just manually rewrite and polish this draft myself to be safe. Good luck!"
  </p>
  <p>
    You spend the next hour painstakingly rewriting every paragraph in your own voice, ensuring the flow is natural, the arguments are grounded in actual history (referencing NATO and containment), and the language sounds like a human student. It's clean, safe, and written entirely in your own style.
  </p>
  <p>
    Just as you finish editing and prepare to upload, your phone buzzes. It's a text from your close classmate, Sarah:
  </p>
  <p style="color: #a5b4fc; font-style: italic; border-left: 3px solid #a5b4fc; padding-left: 15px; margin: 20px 0;">
    "Hey! Are you done with the history essay? I'm completely stuck, I've had a massive panic attack and my mind is blank. Can I please see your essay just to get some inspiration for how to structure my paragraphs? I promise on my life I won't copy a single word!"
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Share Essay" class="btn btn-purple">Send her your edited AI essay.</a>
