:: Share Essay
<div class="container">
  <h2>A Dangerous Favor</h2>
  <p>
    You feel a deep pang of empathy for Sarah—you know exactly how terrifying that midnight panic feels. You attach the document and send it: "Here is my draft, Sarah. Just use it as an structural guide to get your ideas flowing, okay? Please make sure you don't copy any of the actual phrasing."
  </p>
  <p>
    "OMG thank you so much! You literally saved my life!" she replies with several crying emojis.
  </p>
  <p>
    You submit your polished essay, shut your screen, and sleep. Two days later, you receive a terse, cold email from Professor Vance: *Please visit my office immediately to discuss your essay submission.* When you walk down the history hallway, you see Sarah sitting on a bench outside his door. She is completely pale, staring at the floor, on the verge of tears.
  </p>
  <p>
    "He knows," she whispers to you, her voice trembling. "He has both of our papers on his desk."
