:: Office Confrontation Sarah
<div class="container">
  <h2>Called to the Board</h2>
  <p>
    You and Sarah step into the office, the door closing behind you with a heavy click. Professor Vance is sitting silently behind his mahogany desk. He doesn't look angry; instead, he looks deeply tired and disappointed. Without a word, he slides two printed essays across the desk.
  </p>
  <p>
    "I ran both of your submissions through our department's structural analysis tool," Vance says, his voice quiet but incredibly heavy. "They are 85% identical in sentence length, paragraph transitions, vocabulary, and even citation sequence. Furthermore, both essays contain highly specific, identical syntactic quirks characteristic of machine generation."
  </p>
  <p>
    Sarah looks at you, terror in her eyes, completely silent. She is frozen, waiting for you to say something. The weight of the entire situation presses down on your chest like a lead block.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <a data-passage="Blame Self" class="btn btn-danger">Take the blame: admit you used AI and shared it with her.</a>
