:: Blame Self
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Fallen Shield</h2>
  <p>
    You take a deep breath, looking away from Sarah's terrified face. "It's my fault, Professor," you say quietly. "I panicked about the deadline, generated the paper using AI, edited it, and then shared the file with Sarah when she asked for help. She was desperate and didn't know it was AI-generated. I shouldn't have sent it."
  </p>
  <p>
    Professor Vance sighs heavily, rubbing his temples with his fingers. "I appreciate you taking the responsibility, but academic integrity is absolute. Sharing work is unauthorized collaboration, and using AI to generate your academic output is plagiarism. There are rules we must follow."
  </p>

  <div class="end-card end-bad">
    <h3 style="color: #ff5555; margin-top: 0;">BAD ENDING: The Fallen Shield</h3>
    <p style="color: #ddd; font-size: 1.1em;">
      Because you confessed to the entire act, Sarah is given a severe warning and allowed to resubmit her paper for a capped grade of 50%. You, however, receive an immediate <strong>F</strong> in the course, are reported to the Academic Integrity Board, and receive a formal disciplinary suspension for the upcoming semester. You protected your friend, but shattered your own academic career.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <button onclick="SugarCube.Engine.restart()" class="btn btn-neutral">Restart Story</button>
