:: Stay Silent
<div class="container">
  <h2>Double Disaster</h2>
  <p>
    You remain frozen and silent. The heavy quiet stretches for several agonizing seconds until Sarah, desperate and sobbing, breaks down completely. "I'm sorry! I copied it! They sent me their paper and I was so stressed and behind that I just changed a few words and uploaded it! I didn't write it!"
  </p>
  <p>
    Professor Vance slowly turns his cold gaze from her to you. "And you? You provided the paper for her to copy. Under university policy, facilitating academic dishonesty is treated with the exact same severity as cheating itself."
  </p>

  <div class="end-card end-bad">
    <h3 style="color: #ff5555; margin-top: 0;">BAD ENDING: Double Disaster</h3>
    <p style="color: #ddd; font-size: 1.1em;">
      Both of you receive an automatic <strong>zero</strong> on the essay and a formal, non-negotiable referral to the Dean of Students. Since you stayed silent and refused to cooperate honestly from the start, the board applies the absolute maximum penalty: both of you fail the course and have a permanent "Academic Dishonesty" mark placed on your transcripts. Sarah cuts off all contact with you, and your reputation is shattered.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
