:: Final Exam Unprepared
<div class="container">
  <h2>The Price of Bypassing</h2>
  <p>
    It is the end of the semester. You sit in the massive, quiet gymnasium for the final exam. No Wi-Fi, no devices, no chat boxes. Just a wooden desk, a blue booklet, and a pen.
  </p>
  <p style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 4px solid #ff5555; font-style: italic;">
    <strong>Prompt:</strong> "Discuss the geopolitical impact of the Truman Doctrine and explain how containment shaped post-war Europe."
  </p>
  <p>
    You stare at the blank lines. A cold sweat breaks out on your forehead.
  </p>
  <p>
    You realize with a sinking horror that you know absolutely nothing. The AI did all the heavy lifting for you all semester, and you edited it without absorbing a single detail. You can't remember what the Truman Doctrine was. You don't know the difference between containment and NATO. Your mind is as blank as the page.
  </p>

  <div id="grade-reveal" style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <button onclick="window.revealGrade()" class="btn btn-danger">Hand in the blank booklet...</button>
  </div>
</div>
